        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>A Shared Propensity Towards Food & Alcohol</title>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" id=\"MathJax-script\" async\n  src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\">\n</script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;\n    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #d9d9d9 0, #d9d9d9 1px, #eeeeee 1px, #eeeeee 12px);\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 20px;\n    color: #222;\n  }\n  .page {\n    max-width: 1060px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: #eeeeee;\n    padding: 24px 30px;\n  }\n  h1.title {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 40px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    margin: 0 0 20px 0;\n    color: #111;\n  }\n  .grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;\n    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n    grid-template-areas:\n      \"background method results\"\n      \"alcohol   method conclusion\";\n    gap: 10px 22px;\n  }\n  .col-background { grid-area: background; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }\n  .col-method { grid-area: method; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }\n  .col-results { grid-area: results; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }\n  .col-alcohol { grid-area: alcohol; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }\n  .col-conclusion { grid-area: conclusion; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }\n\n  .section-header {\n    background: #111;\n    color: #fff;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 19px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    padding: 10px 0;\n    margin-bottom: 14px;\n  }\n  .section-body {\n    background: #fff;\n    padding: 14px 18px 20px 18px;\n    flex: 1;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n  }\n  .col-method .section-body { padding-bottom: 14px; }\n\n  /* BACKGROUND STATS */\n  .stat-row {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    margin: 14px 0;\n  }\n  .stat-num {\n    font-size: 34px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    width: 90px;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n  }\n  .stat-icon {\n    font-size: 26px;\n    width: 40px;\n    text-align: center;\n    flex-shrink: 0;\n  }\n  .stat-label { font-size: 13px; margin-left: 6px; }\n\n  /* ALCOHOL IS LIKE FOOD */\n  .icon-row {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: flex-start;\n    gap: 22px;\n    font-size: 30px;\n    margin-bottom: 14px;\n  }\n  ul { margin: 6px 0 0 0; padding-left: 18px; }\n  li { margin-bottom: 8px; }\n\n  /* METHOD */\n  .method-list li { margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  .chart-title { font-weight: 700; margin: 16px 0 10px 0; font-size: 13px; }\n  .bar-row {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n    font-size: 12px;\n  }\n  .bar-label { width: 45px; text-align: right; margin-right: 6px; color: #333; }\n  .bar-track {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 16px;\n    border-left: 1px solid #333;\n    flex-grow: 0;\n  }\n  .bar-fill {\n    height: 16px;\n    background: #ccc;\n    border: 1px solid #333;\n  }\n  .bar-fill.dark { background: #111; }\n  .bar-pct { margin-left: 6px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px; }\n  .sub-heading { font-weight: 700; margin-top: 16px; font-size: 13px; }\n\n  /* RESULTS TABLE */\n  table {\n    width: 100%;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    margin-top: 4px;\n  }\n  th, td {\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    padding: 6px 8px;\n    text-align: left;\n  }\n  thead th {\n    background: #888;\n    color: #fff;\n    font-weight: 600;\n  }\n  tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #f2f2f2; }\n  .icon-heads {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: center;\n    gap: 60px;\n    margin: 30px 0 10px 0;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    width: 90px;\n    height: 90px;\n    border: 2px solid #333;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    text-align: center;\n    color: #444;\n    padding: 4px;\n  }\n\n  /* CONCLUSION */\n  .col-conclusion .section-header { margin-top: 0; }\n  .col-conclusion .section-body p { margin: 0 0 12px 0; }\n\n  footer {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    margin-top: 16px;\n    padding-top: 12px;\n  }\n  .footer-left {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 14px;\n  }\n  .grad-icon {\n    font-size: 34px;\n  }\n  .footer-left div.school {\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n  }\n  .footer-right {\n    text-align: right;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    color: #333;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n  <h1 class=\"title\">A SHARED PROPENSITY TOWARDS FOOD &amp; ALCOHOL</h1>\n\n  <div class=\"grid\">\n\n    <!-- BACKGROUND -->\n    <div class=\"col-background\">\n      <div class=\"section-header\">BACKGROUND</div>\n      <div class=\"section-body\">\n        <p>Overeating and binge drinking are two of the most common health problems among college students:</p>\n\n        <div class=\"stat-row\">\n          <div class=\"stat-num\">48%</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-icon\">🍔</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-label\">report binge eating problems</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"stat-row\">\n          <div class=\"stat-num\">63%</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-icon\">⚨</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-label\">of females report binge drinking episodes</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"stat-row\">\n          <div class=\"stat-num\">85%</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-icon\">♂</div>\n          <div class=\"stat-label\">of males report binge drinking episodes</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- METHOD & MEASURES -->\n    <div class=\"col-method\">\n      <div class=\"section-header\">METHOD &amp; MEASURES</div>\n      <div class=\"section-body\">\n        <p>200 UCLA Undergraduates (76% females, Mean Age - 22.1) filled out an online survey in one-sitting as part of a longer experimental study with the following exclusionary criteria:</p>\n\n        <ul class=\"method-list\">\n          <li>Less than 21 years old</li>\n          <li>Self-reported history of eating disorders or substance abuse</li>\n          <li>Abstinence from drinking beer</li>\n          <li>A strict diet and food allergies to experimental stimuli</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"chart-title\"># of times alcohol was consumed with a meal / month:</div>\n\n        <div class=\"bar-row\">\n          <div class=\"bar-label\">Under 5</div>\n          <div class=\"bar-track\"><div class=\"bar-fill\" style=\"width:60px;\"></div></div>\n          <div class=\"bar-pct\">13%</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"bar-row\">\n          <div class=\"bar-label\">5-10</div>\n          <div class=\"bar-track\"><div class=\"bar-fill\" style=\"width:110px;\"></div></div>\n          <div class=\"bar-pct\">25%</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"bar-row\">\n          <div class=\"bar-label\">11-20</div>\n          <div class=\"bar-track\"><div class=\"bar-fill dark\" style=\"width:185px;\"></div></div>\n          <div class=\"bar-pct\">42%</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"bar-row\">\n          <div class=\"bar-label\">Over 20</div>\n          <div class=\"bar-track\"><div class=\"bar-fill dark\" style=\"width:90px;\"></div></div>\n          <div class=\"bar-pct\">20%</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"sub-heading\">Alcohol Expectancy Questionnaire (AEQ)</div>\n        <p>A questionnaire measuring one's anticipatory effects of drinking and consuming alcohol.</p>\n\n        <div class=\"sub-heading\">Dutch Eating Behavior Questionnaire (DEBQ)</div>\n        <p>A questionnaire assessing one's eating behaviors (since expectancies predict consumption, food expectancies are implicitly implied).</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- RESULTS -->\n    <div class=\"col-results\">\n      <div class=\"section-header\">RESULTS</div>\n      <div class=\"section-body\">\n        <table>\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th>AEQ / DEBQ</th>\n              <th>External</th>\n              <th>Emotional</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td>Relaxation &amp; Tension Reduction</td>\n              <td>320</td>\n              <td>240</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td>Arousal &amp; Aggression</td>\n              <td>240</td>\n              <td>220</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td>Increased Social Assertiveness</td>\n              <td>250</td>\n              <td>169</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td>Physical &amp; Social Pleasure</td>\n              <td>210</td>\n              <td>114</td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n\n        <div class=\"icon-heads\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Icon: head with flower/brain]</div>\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Icon: head with cloud]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ALCOHOL IS LIKE FOOD -->\n    <div class=\"col-alcohol\">\n      <div class=\"section-header\">ALCOHOL IS LIKE FOOD</div>\n      <div class=\"section-body\">\n        <div class=\"icon-row\">\n          <span>🍷</span><span>🍽</span><span>🥃</span>\n        </div>\n        <ul>\n          <li>Alcohol is derived from sugar - similar chemical bases as food.</li>\n          <li>Both eating and drinking alcohol activate dopaminergic pathways in the human brain.</li>\n          <li>Addiction models have been applied to both food and alcohol use, as well as correlations between food and alcohol intake conducted in animal studies.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- CONCLUSION -->\n    <div class=\"col-conclusion\">\n      <div class=\"section-header\">CONCLUSION</div>\n      <div class=\"section-body\">\n        <p><strong>The results support our hypothesis that: Food expectancy is positively correlated to alcohol expectancy.</strong></p>\n        <p>DEBQ External eating scale correlated to all AEQ scales, while DEBQ Emotional Eating scale only correlated to some AEQ scales.</p>\n        <p><strong>External eating</strong> had a more consistent relationship with alcohol expectancies, where <strong>Emotional eating</strong> had a less consistent relationship.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  <footer>\n    <div class=\"footer-left\">\n      <span class=\"grad-icon\">🎓</span>\n      <div class=\"school\">University of New York,<br>New York</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"footer-right\">\n      STUDY CONDUCTED BY: Carla Ramirez, Francis R. Griffon and Elena Takiyoma, UNIVERSITY OF NEW YORK<br>\n      RESOURCES: Walsh, Kathy.  Chen, Anthony. \"The psychology of consumption and stress\" The Pearson Journal, 2017 // Saluda, Mariana. Ternitope, Janet. \"Neuroscience of addiction and pleasure\" The Science Review, 2018. // Jurgen, Hans. Lee, Penelope. \"Consumption, Pleasure and Empowerment\", The Arch Journal, 2020.\n    </div>\n  </footer>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
